            },
            {
                "name": "Note_0",
                "type": "digsim.circuit.components.Note",
                "display_name": "Note",
                "settings": {
                    "text": "Memory arbiter. The ILM (instruction fetch) and the DLM (loads and stores) share the ROM\nand the RAM. When both want the same memory, the ILM reads the instruction first while\nthe DLM waits (dlm_ready = 0). The phase flip-flop then gives the DLM the memory for one\ncycle, and the processor sees the instruction held in insn_latch.\nowns_ram and owns_rom: the ILM uses that memory in this cycle (ilm_ram is 1 for the RAM).\nram_re is 1 while the RAM is not written."
                }
            }
        ]
    },
